---
import Base from '#layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '#lib/site';

const locale = 'en';
// Stable "last updated" — bump by hand when the policy text changes, so the
// date reflects real revisions, not the build clock.
const updated = '17 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · argot"
  description="argot runs entirely on your machine — no telemetry, no accounts, and your code never leaves your computer."
  locale={locale}
>
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-line bg-bg/80 backdrop-blur-md">
    <div class="mx-auto flex h-16 max-w-3xl items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5" aria-label="argot — home">
        <span class="wordmark text-lg">ar<span class="g">g</span>ot</span>
        <span class="rounded-md border border-line px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted"
          >privacy</span
        >
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 sm:gap-3">
        <a
          href="/docs/"
          class="rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 text-sm text-ink-dim transition-colors hover:text-ink"
          >Docs</a
        >
        <a
          href={SITE.github}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="rounded-md border border-line bg-panel/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm transition-colors hover:border-line-2"
          >GitHub ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
      argot processes your code entirely on your machine. It does not collect, transmit, or store
      your source code, your git history, or anything derived from them — and there is no account and
      no telemetry.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <section class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The short version</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          argot is a local command-line tool. It reads your code and git history on your own computer
          to build a per-repo model, and runs every check against that local model. Nothing is
          uploaded, and no one — including argot's maintainers — receives your code, your findings, or
          usage data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What we don't collect</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 text-ink-dim">
          <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-ember">—</span> No telemetry, usage analytics, or crash reporting.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-ember">—</span> No account, login, or personal identifiers.</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-ember">—</span> No source code, snippets, or scan results ever leave your machine.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Network activity</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          The analysis path works fully offline. The binary can make outbound requests in the
          following cases — none upload your code, git history, findings, or usage data:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col gap-3 text-ink-dim">
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-ember">—</span>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Model download (once, optional).</strong> The first
              time the semantic checks run, argot fetches a code-embedding model (~100&nbsp;MB,
              checksum-pinned) from its public release host to a local cache
              (<code class="text-ink">~/.cache/argot/models</code>). This downloads a file; it uploads
              nothing.</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-ember">—</span>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Version check (at most once a day).</strong>
              argot fetches a small version file to tell you if a newer release exists — a plain request
              with no code and no identifiers. Turn it off with <code class="text-ink">check = false</code>
              under <code class="text-ink">[update]</code> in <code class="text-ink">argot.toml</code>
              (or <code class="text-ink">ARGOT_UPDATE_CHECK=0</code>).</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span class="text-ember">—</span>
            <span
              ><strong class="font-medium text-ink">Installation.</strong> The curl installer and npm
              fetch the binary from GitHub Releases / npm, under their own privacy terms.</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          Set <code class="text-ink">ARGOT_OFFLINE=1</code> to forbid all network access: argot then
          skips the model download and the update check entirely, and says so rather than failing
          silently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Continuous integration</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          The argot GitHub Action runs inside your own CI. It fits the model and checks the diff on
          your runners, reads the pull-request diff through GitHub's API with your token, and writes
          the results back to your PR. Nothing is sent to argot's maintainers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The Claude Code plugin & MCP server</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          The <a href="/docs/plugin/" class="text-ember hover:text-ember-bright">plugin</a> runs your
          local <code class="text-ink">argot</code> binary. The MCP server answers your coding agent
          with statistics derived from your local repository, on your machine. Neither transmits your
          code off your computer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">This website</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          argot.tmonier.com is a static site with no analytics, no tracking pixels, and no advertising
          or tracking cookies. It is served by Cloudflare Pages, which may keep standard server request
          logs (such as IP address, timestamp, and requested URL) for security and operation under
          Cloudflare's own terms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes & contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
          We may update this policy; the date above marks the latest revision, and its full history is
          public in the argot repository. Questions or a privacy request? Email{' '}
          <a href="mailto:support@tmonier.com" class="text-ember hover:text-ember-bright">support@tmonier.com</a>,
          or open an issue on{' '}
          <a href={SITE.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-ember hover:text-ember-bright">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
